  <accessrestrict id="2813f134f7d514d73714321e552aa5e1">
    <head>Conditions Governing Access</head>
<p>Open for research with select materials restricted as noted. Brittle or damaged items are available at the discretion of RAC.</p>  </accessrestrict>
  <userestrict id="bd4c1e565913c4aa60784cbd3254fe57">
    <head>Conditions Governing Use</head>
<p>Collection is open for research. If accessing the records of the Population Council, I understand that I am given access to these records on condition that I will not identify by name, either in my research notes or in publication or recording, the names of individuals who received or apparently received medical diagnoses and/or treatments, whose case(s), may be documented or mentioned by personal name in the Population Council records.</p>  </userestrict>
  <userestrict id="2e13045f3e8bfd1ffe8ce59013d5f199">
    <head>Conditions Governing Use</head>
<p>The Population Council retains title, copyright and literary rights in the collection, in so far as it holds them.</p><p>The Rockefeller Archive Center has authority to grant permission to cite and publish material from the collection. The Population Council retains the right to prior consent with respect to any reproduction or extensive quotation of the records for publication.</p><p>Reproduction/duplication of archival items is routinely provided in accordance with "fair use". If the RAC does not hold copyright for an archival collection, or items within a collection, it is the users responsibility to contact the copyright holder, or make a fair effort to do so, prior to publication.</p>  </userestrict>
  <scopecontent id="85438581237922aea0a16b448f71f7f8">
    <head>Scope and Contents</head>
<p>The Miscellaneous Files document a wide variety of subject matter and file types including but not limited to meeting records, lectures, receptions and events, real estate files, planning and proposal documents, field staff and trip files. There is also a small selection of Taiwan files including correspondence and reports.</p>  </scopecontent>
  <arrangement id="1a5586dd618f1e5b229130aeb38ef55f">
    <head>Arrangement</head>
<p>Original order is maintained, as received.</p>  </arrangement>
